Q: How to round the AVG() value from a CodeIgniter query A: <p>You can call <code>number_format()</code> on the lone returned value from your query if you want a formatted string with thousands placeholders otherwise use <code>round()</code> to return a float value.</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>public function getAveRating(int $restoid): float
{ 
    return round(
        $this-&gt;db
            -&gt;select_avg('rate')
            -&gt;get_where('ratings', ['restoid' =&gt; $restoid])
            -&gt;row('rate'),
        2
    );
}
</code></pre>
<p>Or you could round in the query itself.</p>
<pre class="lang-php prettyprint-override"><code>public function getAveRating(int $restoid): float
{ 
    return (float)$this-&gt;db
        -&gt;select('ROUND(AVG(rate), 2) rate')
        -&gt;get_where('ratings', ['restoid' =&gt; $restoid])
        -&gt;row('rate');
}
</code></pre>

